## 10. Create the EF migration

Run: `cd ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker && dotnet ef migrations add AddShipments`

If `dotnet ef` is not available, install it first: `dotnet tool install --global dotnet-ef`

## 11. Add reference to Client project from Server

The server project needs to reference the Client Models namespace. Check if there's already a project reference from ShipmentTracker to ShipmentTracker.Client. If so, great. If not, add one.

## 12. Build and verify

Run `dotnet build` from the solution root to verify everything compiles.

IMPORTANT: Make sure the `Models` directory exists in the Client project before creating files in it. Create directories as needed.

